  "solution": {
    "text": "Reversible isothermal expansion from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;during this process<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;constant</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;constant.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;S</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;Entropy will increase&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PV</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;constant.</p><p>and during adiabatic reversible expansion.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>ve</mi></math></p><p>so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>&nbsp;will decrease</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>nc</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>ve</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>&nbsp;will decrease</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;(isoentropic process)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo></math>constant. and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>pv</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msup><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;constant.</p><p>Keeping in mind&nbsp;correct graph are 1,2 and 4.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
